      "stance": "bullish",
      "mention_type": "explicit_stance",
      "reasons": [
        "largest Western Tungsten producer",
        "rare earth / critical minerals thesis still intact",
        "massive shortages and decoupling from China unchanged",
        "Trump announced over $2B in critical mining projects and $180M for mining workforce education",
        "160 mineral deals totaling nearly $40B since January 2025"
      ],
      "is_risk": false,
      "conviction": "medium",
      "raw_mention": "$ALM",
      "text": "Crazy how the market just forgot about the rare earth / critical minerals thesis.\n\nFeels like the sector suffered the same sentiment collapse as defense recently, but is bouncing back with momentum/growth broadly.\n\nWhen nothing changed in the massive shortages and decoupling from China...\n\nAnd now Trump announced over $2 billion in critical mining projects and $180 million for mining workforce education, building on 160 mineral deals totaling nearly $40 billion since January 2025.\n\nI actually used to publish my rare earth / mining favorites on @joinautopilot but pivoted the fund, and it's still a thesis I have a lot of interest in.\n\nI'm actually interviewing the CEO of $ALM, Lewis Black next week, the largest Western Tungsten producer to talk more about it.\n\nShould be an exciting read through.",
      "url": "https://x.com/michaelsikand/status/2085827658664030261",
